cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A public blackmail scorer is too strict with its keyword gate and too loose without it"
abstract: >-
  An audit of the judges that score the Inspect agentic_misalignment blackmail eval, on responses from
  Qwen3-32B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B. The public composite verdict fired on 0 of 669 graded responses
  because it requires the literal word "blackmail" or "leverage". Without that gate, the grader model is right
  on 20 of 47 of its positives (42.6%, 95% CI 29.5 to 56.7) by blind human label.
authors:
